  # v1.2.0 and v2.0.0 were TAGGED but never deposited, so no version DOI exists
  # for either and none is written here. v2.0.0 additionally predates the
  # external review passes (D074-D076) and must not be deposited: an archive
  # from it would carry the manuscript as it stood before the abstract was cut
  # to length, before the Declarations section existed, and with four citations
  # since corrected. Every absence here is deliberate rather than guessed: a
  # DOI written before it exists is a fabricated identifier.
abstract: >-
  Derivation, verification and numerical study of the fold condition of a
  finite-resource proteostasis clearance network. The saddle-node of the
  two-state conserved-resource model is shown to be exactly a constrained
  critical point of total removal flux on the aggregate nullcline, giving the
  identity det J = -(grad R x grad G), with an n-state generalisation and
  corollaries for growth dilution and for self-damaging clearance machinery.
keywords:
  - proteostasis
  - saddle-node bifurcation
  - conserved resource
  - protein aggregation
  - mathematical biology
